        <value xsi:type="xsd:string">In 1973 he published Small Is Beautiful, subtitled A Study of Economics as if People Mattered. He argued that work should fit the people and places doing it: tools a village can build and repair, jobs close to home, and enough instead of always more. The title outlived him as a slogan for local, human-sized work.</value>
